{ of_string_length.init - a DSEE derived object of
  be_com/backend.ins.pas (cc.a88k only): the initializer of the section
  of_string_length (0x2B712C: 43 words, the lengths of of_string's
  names, by of$t; the section's last two bytes are padding).  Included by lir.pas.

  No Apollo copy survives; reconstructed from the DOMAIN C 6.9 binary
  cc.a88k, the section's bytes (translator PA6).

  How the section is shared (docs/questions.md 161, translator PB2's
  scheme): backend.ins.pas declares the section's variable for every
  unit; this file, included by lir.pas, gives it its initial value with
  a `define' statement (the language reference's section 7.2.2, method
  2).  dpc does not yet lay out such an initialized section named as
  its variable (docs/dpc-gaps.md 32): the gate renames the section.

  Not known from the original: the file's layout. }

